========================================================================
  PART 1: THE DESCENT POLYNOMIAL F(T, x)
========================================================================

  Computing F(T, x) for n=5 tournament classes:
  H=1: F(T,x) = 1x^4
    F(T,1) = 1 = H ✓
    F(T,0) = 0 (paths with no descent)
    F(T,-1) = 1
  H=3: F(T,x) = 2x^3 + 1x^4
    F(T,1) = 3 = H ✓
    F(T,0) = 0 (paths with no descent)
    F(T,-1) = -1
  H=5: F(T,x) = 4x^3 + 1x^4
    F(T,1) = 5 = H ✓
    F(T,0) = 0 (paths with no descent)
    F(T,-1) = -3
  H=9: F(T,x) = 8x^3 + 1x^4
    F(T,1) = 9 = H ✓
    F(T,0) = 0 (paths with no descent)
    F(T,-1) = -7
  H=11: F(T,x) = 10x^3 + 1x^4
    F(T,1) = 11 = H ✓
    F(T,0) = 0 (paths with no descent)
    F(T,-1) = -9
  H=13: F(T,x) = 7x^2 + 6x^3
    F(T,1) = 13 = H ✓
    F(T,0) = 0 (paths with no descent)
    F(T,-1) = 1
  H=15: F(T,x) = 6x^2 + 8x^3 + 1x^4
    F(T,1) = 15 = H ✓
    F(T,0) = 0 (paths with no descent)
    F(T,-1) = -1


